WEBVTT

00:48:57.250 --> 00:49:00.559
and she wrote a profile about me
and she wrote a profile about Adam.

00:49:00.583 --> 00:49:03.434
AG: And when we met and realized this,
my first thought was,

00:49:03.458 --> 00:49:05.226
we need to write a profile of Susan

00:49:05.250 --> 00:49:07.976
based on what we learned
about her from her profiling us,

00:49:08.000 --> 00:49:09.268
which is maybe too meta.

00:49:09.292 --> 00:49:11.143
But she was hoping to be here tonight.

00:49:11.167 --> 00:49:14.393
She could not make it, but she sent in
a question for us to discuss,

00:49:14.417 --> 00:49:16.309
which I thought was really interesting,

00:49:16.333 --> 00:49:18.684
which was, what do we think
about passionate work?

00:49:18.708 --> 00:49:22.268
Is that something we should strive for?
Can you ever have too much of it?

00:49:22.292 --> 00:49:23.976
Do you want to go first?

00:49:24.000 --> 00:49:27.018
EP: I think it's a fascinating
question, actually,

00:49:27.042 --> 00:49:31.351
because passion for a long time
throughout history,